# HR//0D -- line endings + binary handling
#
# NOTE ON GIT LFS (BUG-010): this project does NOT use LFS.
# Reason: pixel-art PNGs and short SFX are small (KB, not GB), and LFS adds a hard requirement that
# every teammate installs the LFS client before cloning -- plus GitHub LFS bandwidth quotas.
# Committing art as normal binary blobs keeps the repo simple and clone-able with nothing extra.
#
# If you ever need LFS back (large PSDs, long audio, video):
#   1. everyone installs Git LFS:  winget install GitHub.GitLFS  &&  git lfs install
#   2. re-add the filter lines below and run:
#      git lfs migrate import --include="*.png,*.psd,*.wav,*.mp3"
#   3. push with --force-with-lease and tell the whole team to re-clone.
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never diff, never convert line endings, never filter.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.psd  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.fbx  binary
*.unity binary
*.asset binary
*.prefab binary
